<title>UK: UK Sept business failures lowest for six years.</title>
<headline>UK Sept business failures lowest for six years.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK accountants Deloitte &amp; Touche said administrative receiverships and administration order appointments in Britain were the lowest for six years in September and were down 42 percent on September 1995:</p>
<p>  BUSINESS FAILURE APPOINTMENTS   SEPT     AUG	     AUG 95</p>
<p> England, Wales and Scotland	  83     122		145</p>
<p> Breakdown by SECTOR		  SEPT    12 MTHS TO SEPT  1995</p>
<p>    Manufacturing industry	    24     482		485</p>
<p>    Construction			  11     320		367</p>
<p>    Finance &amp; business services	7     211		341</p>
<p>  Hotels and catering		  8	83		107</p>
<p>  Retailing			     14     239		269</p>
<p>  Wholesaling			    6     119		144</p>
<p>  Transport &amp; Communications	 5	91		 76</p>
<p>  Other services			 8     169		185</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
